  "name": "Inquisitor Greyfax — Esper Tap/Untap",
  "format": "commander",
  "description": "**Gameplan:** Tap opponents' creatures, get paid for every tap, untap and do it again, then\nconvert \"tapped\" into \"dead\". Greyfax is the engine in the command zone (`{1}, {T}: Tap target\ncreature an opponent controls. Investigate.`) and her team-wide vigilance means your creatures\nattack *and* stay untapped as Opposition fuel. Unwinding Clock is the deck's Seedborn Muse —\nit untaps your artifacts during **each** other player's untap step, and the tappers are\nartifacts, so Icy Manipulator / Hylda's Crown / Staff of Domination fire four times per round\ninstead of once. Every one of those taps triggers Hylda, Verity Circle, Sharae and Gideon's\nAvenger. Their board ends up tapped and shrinking under the assassins; yours attacks without\never opening up. See research/gameplan.md.",
